#order test/ci-workflow.test.ts
#order docs/installation.md
#order README.md
#order CONTRIBUTING.md
#reason scripts/check-linux-package.sh Proves the zip that would ship holds the binaries, keeps them executable and has RunAsNode off.
#reason .github/workflows/ci.yml Makes the ubuntu leg prove the Linux package builds and is complete, not just compiles.
#reason .github/workflows/release.yml Builds, checks and uploads the Linux zip so a v* tag publishes it beside the others.
#reason CONTRIBUTING.md Lists the Linux build command with the other platform builds.
#reason README.md Adds the Linux download and how to run it beside the macOS and Windows entries.
#reason docs/installation.md Tells Linux users how to download and run the unsigned zip and the sandbox workaround.
#reason package.json Adds the Linux build and zip commands so CI and the release build the same package.
#reason scripts/fuses.js Lets the post-package fuse step find the Linux binary instead of only macOS and Windows.
#reason scripts/package-licences.mjs Names linux in the usage line so the licence step is documented for the new platform.
#reason test/ci-workflow.test.ts Keeps the CI workflow guard true now that the ubuntu leg packages.
#reason test/licences.test.ts Pins the Linux resources folder the licence step writes into.
#reason test/release-workflow.test.ts Expects the Linux zip among the release uploads so a dropped job fails.
#reason test/updater-service.test.ts Pins that Linux only offers the release page and never asks the macOS feed.
#story A Linux user downloads Lantern from a release
#step actor Maintainer
#step action pushes a v* tag to release
#file .github/workflows/release.yml
#file package.json
#step subject the Linux x64 package
#below actor Linux user
#below interaction can download, extract and run the zip
#file docs/installation.md
#file README.md
#below consequence no Linux download existed => Lantern-linux-x64.zip is on the release
#file scripts/fuses.js
#file scripts/package-licences.mjs
#story Contributors see the Linux package checked on every push
#step actor Contributor
#step action pushes a branch to
#step subject the CI build on Ubuntu
#file .github/workflows/ci.yml
#below actor Contributor
#below interaction sees a red build if the zip is incomplete
#file scripts/check-linux-package.sh
#below consequence Ubuntu only compiled the app => Ubuntu builds, zips and checks it
#file test/ci-workflow.test.ts
#file test/release-workflow.test.ts
#file test/licences.test.ts
#file test/updater-service.test.ts
